			"Message": "docs(Echo): Add Parameters/Returns sections and tighten Rustdoc across core sources\n\nStandardize the inline documentation across Echo's core source files — Library, Queue, Scheduler, Worker, and Task modules — with:\n\n- New `## Parameters` and `## Returns` sections on all public methods, clarifying argument semantics and return values\n- Tighter doc descriptions that shift from explanatory narrative to declarative intent (e.g., \"This method implements the complete work-finding logic\" → \"Implements the complete work-finding logic\")\n- Module-level headings normalized to `# Name` format without redundant \"Enum\" / \"Struct\" suffixes\n- Doc list punctuation alignment (trailing hyphens replaced with em-dashes in Library.rs)\n\nNo functional changes — documentation only.",
